# A drain that waits instead of fencing. The close records the allocator head
# without re-claiming the author's epoch, so a write admitted before the close
# and delivered after it is allocated above the recorded head; the owner re-arms
# below it and passes it. Waiting for every admitted write to return is the same
# thing in this model: a call returns by timeout while its append is still
# delivered.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestDrainWithoutFence
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the close records the head without fencing out writes admitted before it
PERTURBS: Close

--- FIND
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no fence: the shard's entry for the author is not raised.
    /\ fFence' = fFence
--- END
